{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And those coming, male and female,</b> its sense: those coming into the ark." "And the sense of \"and YHWH shut him in\": it is for praise, for closing at this time is better than opening, while at another time it is for reproach — \"He shuts in upon a man\" (Job 12:14), \"and Elohim hedged him about\" (Job 3:23) — and the proof is the beginning of the verse. Now behold, the opening was closed, and HaShem helped him so that no place in the ark was opened, for immediately they would all have died. Now it has already been written, \"and the rain was upon the earth forty days and forty nights\"; if so, what is the sense of \"and the flood was upon the earth forty days\"? Its explanation is thus: when the flood was forty days upon the earth, the waters increased and lifted the ark and it rose above the earth. And this is a sign, that for forty days it did not move from its place."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:41.721698389Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}